{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-tangent","title":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":629,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:horizontal-lift-tangent","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-linear]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent","line":1022,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The horizontal lift of a tangent vector]\n\\label{def:horizontal-lift-tangent}\n\n\\uses{def:horizontal-lift-linear, def:horizontal-space, def:submersion}\n\n\n\n\nFor a smooth submersion $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ with metric $\\tilde g$, the horizontal lift at $x$ is $L_x:T_{\\pi(x)}M\\to T_x\\tilde M$ obtained from Definition \\ref{def:horizontal-lift-linear} with $B=\\tilde g_x$ and $A=d\\pi_x$. It is the unique map with $d\\pi_xL_xu=u$ and $L_xu\\in H_x$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The horizontal lift of a tangent vector] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d74616e67656e74\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear\">↗ def:horizontal-lift-linear</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiema