e horizontal lift of a tangent vector]\n\\label{def:horizontal-lift-tangent}\n\n\\uses{def:horizontal-lift-linear, def:horizontal-space, def:submersion}\n\n\n\n\nFor a smooth submersion $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ with metric $\\tilde g$, the horizontal lift at $x$ is $L_x:T_{\\pi(x)}M\\to T_x\\tilde M$ obtained from Definition \\ref{def:horizontal-lift-linear} with $B=\\tilde g_x$ and $A=d\\pi_x$. It is the unique map with $d\\pi_xL_xu=u$ and $L_xu\\in H_x$.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-linear","title":"def:horizontal-lift-linear","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion","title":"def:submersion","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}